<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Mathematics on emsenn.net</title><link>https://emsenn.net/tags/mathematics/</link><description>Recent content in Mathematics on emsenn.net</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 04 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://emsenn.net/tags/mathematics/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>The Four Mathematical Universes</title><link>https://emsenn.net/blog/2026-03-04-the-four-mathematical-universes/</link><pubDate>Wed, 04 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://emsenn.net/blog/2026-03-04-the-four-mathematical-universes/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Somewhere in the emsemioverse we should document the relationship that &lt;a href="https://emsenn.net/search/#q=relationality&amp;amp;reference=unpublished" class="link-related" data-note-reference="../../relationality/index.md" aria-label="relationality — search published writing; this note is not published here" title="Search published writing; this note is not published here"&gt;relationality&lt;span aria-hidden="true" data-pagefind-ignore&gt; 🔎&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is formalized as two mathematical systems, &lt;a href="https://emsenn.net/search/#q=semiotic&amp;#43;universes&amp;amp;reference=unpublished" class="link-related" data-note-reference="../../mathematics/objects/universes/semiotic-universe/index.md" aria-label="semiotic universes — search published writing; this note is not published here" title="Search published writing; this note is not published here"&gt;semiotic universes&lt;span aria-hidden="true" data-pagefind-ignore&gt; 🔎&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://emsenn.net/search/#q=quasicrystalline&amp;#43;hypertensor&amp;#43;topos&amp;amp;reference=unpublished" class="link-related" data-note-reference="../../mathematics/objects/topoi/quasicrystalline-hypertensor-topos/index.md" aria-label="quasicrystalline hypertensor topos — search published writing; this note is not published here" title="Search published writing; this note is not published here"&gt;quasicrystalline hypertensor topos&lt;span aria-hidden="true" data-pagefind-ignore&gt; 🔎&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;a href="https://emsenn.net/search/#q=GFRTU&amp;amp;reference=unpublished" class="link-related" data-note-reference="../../mathematics/objects/universes/generative-fibered-recognition-trace-universe/index.md" aria-label="GFRTU — search published writing; this note is not published here" title="Search published writing; this note is not published here"&gt;GFRTU&lt;span aria-hidden="true" data-pagefind-ignore&gt; 🔎&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is meant to be deprecated — as long as we capture all the ideas from it within the QCHTTopos that superseded it, historically in my research.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>